  introDialogue: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2b51582647a3f8340ac72eb350384322, type: 2}
  questionResponses:
  - question: Where are you coming from?
    earlyDaysAnswer: The parish above the north ridge. Road was clear. Dog stayed home.
    midDaysAnswer: The ridge. Walked the fence on the way down. My dog's still missing.
    finalDaysAnswer: The eastern slope. Left food at the east gate again. He hasn't come.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: My flat behind the bread factory. Town all my life. Mountains bore me.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: My wife's house. She keeps it warm. She never minded the quiet.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: The parish. The dog walked down with me. He's waiting by your gate.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  - question: Are you experiencing any symptoms?
    earlyDaysAnswer: I sleep poorly. Always have. Otherwise, no.
    midDaysAnswer: I hear things at night. The wind, probably. I write until it stops.
    finalDaysAnswer: Heavy hands. I write through it. The words always come anyway.
    mismatchEarlyDaysAnswer: None. I sleep like a child. Nothing keeps me awake.
    mismatchMidDaysAnswer: No complaints. I've stopped writing entirely, so I sleep well.
    mismatchFinalDaysAnswer: Nothing. I'm barely thirty. The body keeps up on the mountain.
    uncannyEarlyDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyMidDaysAnswer: 
    uncannyFinalDaysAnswer: 
    cameraTrigger: 
  idleBarks:
    earlyDays:
    - I write when I can't sleep. Lately I can't sleep much.
    - Quiet suits me. I don't say that as a complaint.
    midDays:
    - The mountain has changed. Something about the way it sits now.
    - My dog's been gone nearly two weeks. I don't know where.
    finalDays:
    - I've been leaving food outside the east gate. He hasn't come.
    - The words never came from me. I was only ever the hand.
    uncannyEarlyDays: []
    uncannyMidDays: []
    uncannyFinalDays: []
  IDNumber: 4819203
